# Format is the following:
# LCN
# list of sentences, one per line
# label: lower_prob <= P(phi) <= upper_prob for Type 1 ; tau=True/False
# label: lower_prob <= P(phi|psi) <= upper_prob for Type 2
# IMPORTANT: pay attention to spaces between 
# also, the empty lines and the ones starting with # are skipped
# Variables: A, B, C, D, E, X, Y

s1: 0.1 <= P(X) <= 0.2
s2: 0.2 <= P(Y) <= 0.3
s3: 0.6 <= P(A | X) <= 0.9
s4: 0.5 <= P(B | Y) <= 0.7 
s5: 0.2 <= P(B | A) <= 0.3
s6: 0.4 <= P(C | B) <= 0.6
s7: 0.5 <= P(D | C) <= 0.7
s8: 0.3 <= P(B | D) <= 0.5
s9: 0.5 <= P(E | C) <= 0.7


